{
  "kanji": "匹",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 匹\ntitle: small-animal counter; equal\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 4\nradical: 匸\nradicalNumber: 23\nonyomi: [ヒツ]\nkunyomi: [ひき]\ndistractors: [四, 西, 北]\n---\n\n# 匹 — small-animal counter; equal\n\n**Strokes:** 4 · **Key (radical):** 匸 (no. 23) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n匹 is a counter for small animals when read ひき. In 匹敵 ひってき it instead contributes the idea of matching or equaling. A counter reading and a compound reading serve different purposes.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Imagine the right-open outer enclosure around two small leg-like strokes, like a small animal in a pen.\n\nThe canonical indexing radical is 匸, the outer enclosure open on the right. The inner spreading strokes are not its radical.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ヒツ | on | [匹敵](../words/匹敵.md) ひってき - be a match for; equal; ヒツ becomes ひっ in this compound |\n| ひき | kun | 匹 ひき - counter for small animals; e.g. 二匹 にひき, two small animals |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [匹敵](../words/匹敵.md) ひってき - be a match for; equal\n- 匹 ひき - counter for small animals\n\n## Notes\n\n- Counter pronunciations change with the number: 一匹 いっぴき, one small animal; 二匹 にひき, two; 三匹 さんびき, three. These illustrate ぴき, ひき and びき; do not simply append unchanged ひき to every number.\n- 匹敵する ひってきする compares someone or something with a match or equal; it does not count animals. Learn the small っ in that whole word.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1487250, 1583370.\n\nUsage evidence: [Tofugu: pronunciation of the counter 匹](https://www.tofugu.com/japanese/japanese-counter-hiki/#pronunciation-of-japanese-counter-).\n",
